# Tencent Video persist-conn WebSocket isolation test - v1
# Based on 腾讯4.har analysis (2026-09-04)
#
# EXPERIMENT ONLY — do not merge into stable rules yet.
#
# Purpose:
#   Test whether Tencent Video's persistent WebSocket channel participates in
#   restoring or refreshing the remaining GDT ad-object pool that survives the
#   stable MVL filtering.
#
# Target observed in HAR:
#   https://persist-conn.video.qq.com/ws_proxy
#   HTTP 101 Switching Protocols
#
# Test conditions:
#   1) Enable the stable tencent-video-mvl-v1.snippet.
#   2) Enable this snippet as the ONLY new variable.
#   3) Disable MVL tombstone / IACC experiments / Advertising.list.
#   4) Do NOT clear Tencent Video cache and do NOT reinstall the app.
#   5) Fully kill Tencent Video, then cold-start it.
#
# Interpretation:
#   A) Remaining GDT ads stop appearing/rotating while normal functions work
#      -> persist-conn likely participates in ad-pool restore/refresh.
#   B) Ads remain normal
#      -> persist-conn can be largely excluded for this ad path.
#   C) Ads disappear but normal real-time features also fail
#      -> mixed-purpose channel; host-wide blocking is not suitable as a final rule.
#
# The HAR records the WebSocket upgrade as HTTPS + HTTP 101, so reject the
# handshake request itself before the persistent connection is established.

^https?:\/\/persist-conn\.video\.qq\.com\/ws_proxy(?:\?.*)?$ url reject

hostname = persist-conn.video.qq.com
